Z||000006||William||12-03-2000||11:02 PM||||Shiner, I think you have the plan. I too have considered the black / tan combo! Just changing the brown to black would be a much much easier job. It looks fine in the ferrari and it would give alot of options. The carpet could be black or tan, the seats coud be either or even a black and tan two tone. The tan peices and belts won't have to be touched. I think this could be done with a factory looking job. The only thing to determine is if the brown dash top and center sections should be painted or can they be recovered in leather or vinyl at a shop? Mr Mike WILL NOT cover these items anymore. He did state that new leather items will be released in January. I hope he'll have something to redo these parts with. I'll need to make some calls I guess.<p>[This message has been edited by William (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||11:28 PM||||  William, I just did my intire dash, gauge cluster and my inerior trim will get done tomorrow. It's easy to do your self. I went with charcoal and Presidio gray. It turned out awesome. I might have some pics to post tomorrow. I have a proccess that is fail proof and looks totaly proffesional. E-Mail me if you are interested. Black would probably be the easiest of all to do really. Hard to screw up with black. My Mr. Mikes seats should look awesome when I install them. Hopefully over christmas. Drop me a note.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
